+# TDD task list: caller-scoped memory and meeting authority
+
+**Issue:** `bdd55b7e-2acb-43a4-847d-55a2acb11571`
+**Consumes:** `plan.md`
+**Stage:** Awaiting plan review
+**Rule:** Each task is RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR, then spec review and quality
+review. Stop if a decision would widen authority or alter an approved boundary.
+
+## Task 1 - Lock the cross-domain access-origin contract
+
+**Goal:** Define the product-owned identifiers and denial invariants before any
+schema or repository change.
+
+**Likely files:**
+
+- `packages/contracts/src/conversation.js`
+- `packages/contracts/src/meeting.js`
+- `packages/contracts/contracts/conversation.json`
+- `packages/contracts/contracts/meeting.json`
+- `packages/contracts/src/conversation.test.ts`
+- new/focused meeting contract tests
+
+**OWNS:** `packages/contracts/src/conversation.js`,
+`packages/contracts/src/meeting.js`,
+`packages/contracts/contracts/conversation.json`,
+`packages/contracts/contracts/meeting-runtime-config.json`,
+`packages/contracts/src/conversation.test.ts`,
+`packages/contracts/src/index.test.ts`, `packages/contracts/src/index.d.ts`
+
+**RED:** Add contract tests proving that a meeting access origin is a canonical
+conversation; caller actor identity is server-derived; participant labels and
+providers are non-authoritative; derivatives must preserve tenant plus access
+origin; and a run is evidence, never an actor.
+
+**GREEN:** Extend the existing contracts with the minimum access-origin and
+declassification vocabulary. Reuse actor/membership roles and existing owning
+domain references; do not add a second ACL matrix.
+
+**REFACTOR/verify:** Regenerate/check contract projections through the existing
+contract tooling and run focused contract tests plus lint/type checks.
+
+**Exit evidence:** Exact contract invariants, failing and passing test output,
+generated-drift result, and explicit confirmation that no provider field grants
+access.
+
+**Task commit:** `contracts: define meeting access origins`
+
