+
+**Goal:** Persist one same-tenant meeting conversation and mandatory access
+origins for meeting-derived data without widening existing visibility.
+
+**Likely files:**
+
+- `apps/meeting-api/backend/alembic/versions/0006_caller_scoped_meetings.py`
+- `apps/meeting-api/backend/db.py`
+- `packages/db/src/schema.ts`
+- `packages/db/migrations/0019_caller_access_origins.sql`
+- `packages/db/src/schema.test.ts`
+- `apps/meeting-api/backend/alembic/__tests__/env.test.py`
+
+**OWNS:** all files listed above.
+
+**RED:** Add migration/schema tests for same-tenant composite references,
+incompatible memory visibility/origin combinations, mandatory origins for
+meeting-sourced memories/chunks/proposals, and rejection of cross-tenant links.
+Add a fixture with unresolved legacy derivatives and assert it is quarantined,
+not made org-visible.
+
+**GREEN:** Add `meetings.conversation_id`; a conversation memory visibility
+lane plus `access_conversation_id`; access-origin columns on knowledge chunks
+and proposals; indexes/checks/foreign keys; and a staged owner-only backfill.
+Create a conversation plus owner-admin membership for existing meetings. Link
+only deterministically recoverable derivatives. Record unresolved identifiers
+and counts without content and make all read paths deny them.
+
+**REFACTOR/verify:** Run migration parity, upgrade/downgrade tests, DB contract
+tests, schema tests, and a dry-run inventory on fixtures. Confirm rollback never
+restores permissive legacy grants.
+
+**Exit evidence:** Migration IDs/checksums, row counts by linked/quarantined
+state, RED/GREEN output, and no orphan/cross-tenant access origins.
+
+**Task commit:** `db: add caller-scoped meeting access origins`
+
